# The candidate artifact is content-addressed by SHA-256 and MUST be stored byte-exact.
# Without this, core.autocrlf normalisation changes the published bytes and public
# SHA verification fails. Do not remove.
index.html -text
# 2026-09-02 incident follow-up: index.html references three.min.js via a relative
# <script src> and assets/sfx/** via relative audio-sample fetches. The original publish
# copied only index.html, so three.min.js 404'd, throwing "ReferenceError: THREE is not
# defined" and halting all script execution -- this is why New Game never worked on the
# public deployment. three.min.js is JS text and would otherwise be subject to the same
# CRLF-corruption risk; audio files are binary and git auto-detects them, but marked
# explicitly here for certainty.
three.min.js -text
assets/** -text
